{"school":{"dbn":"30Q230","name":"I.S. 230","boro":"Queens","district":"30","district_label":"District 30","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":956,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"73-10 34 AVENUE, JACKSON HEIGHTS, NY 11372","phone":"718-956-4140","website":"https://is-230.echalksites.com/","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63088","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"Intermediate School 230Q is a zoned middle school in Jackson Heights, Queens. Our student body is diverse, and the vast majority of our students demonstrate an acceptance of individual differences. The school's organizational structure is focused upon continued improvement of instruction. Leadership and faculty implement common core aligned curricula and tasks across grades and content areas, promoting college and career readiness for all students. Starting in grade seven, all students have a choice of Vocal Music, Band or Visual Arts, and receive three periods per week. Most eighth graders take the NYS Regents in Algebra and Living Environment. Eligible eighth graders take the NYC Second Language Proficiency Exam in Spanish to receive HS credit. A wide variety of after school enrichment programs and clubs are available for all interests. Our sixth grade is housed in our Annex building, which is directly across the street from the main building. This smaller environment for grade six helps support students in the social/emotional transition to middle school.","start_time":"8:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"7, E, F to Broadway-74th St; M, R to 65th St","bus":"Q32, Q33, Q47, Q49, Q53-SBS, Q66, Q70-SBS, QM3","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Jackson Heights","latitude":40.752636,"longitude":-73.892871,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.946],"st":["ok"],"n"